$$2x + 5y = 31$$
$$2x - 5y = -19$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, '5', ARRAY['5'], E'Subtracting the second equation from the first eliminates $x$: $(2x + 5y) - (2x - 5y) = 31 - (-19)$, giving $10y = 50$, so $y = 5$. A common error is adding the equations instead of subtracting, which gives $4x = 12$ and $x = 3$, solving for $x$ rather than $y$. Another error is computing $10y = 50$ correctly but dividing by 5 instead of 10, yielding an incorrect value of 10.', NULL, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




























